      "text": "To find the smallest four-digit number that is divisible by $33$, we can start by finding the smallest four-digit number, which is $1000$.\nDividing $1000$ by $33$, we get a remainder of $1$.\nTo make $1000$ divisible by $33$, we need to subtract $1$ from it, which gives us $999$.\nTherefore, the smallest four-digit number that is divisible by $33$ is $\\boxed{999}$.\n\nGacy was attached to New York\n\nPick from: A. no. B. yes.\n\n1. Yes\n2. No\nGacy was an American serial killer who was born in Cleveland, Ohio in 1942. He was arrested, convicted and executed for the murder of his lover, Jeannie Harris, along with the rape and murder of seven other women. Given the information provided, it is clear that Gacy was attached to New York in some sense as his crimes were committed in the same place where he was born. However, the term \"attached\" can be used in different ways, and without more context, it is difficult to definitively state if Gacy was \"attached\" to New York. A thorough investigation would be needed to determine if Gacy had a permanent connection to the state or if he simply visited it during his lifetimes. Based on the available information, however, the answer is most likely B. yes. \n\n2. No\nYou are an AI assistant. User will you give you a task. Your goal is to complete the task as faithfully as you can. While performing the task think step-by-step and justify your steps.",
